# ============================================================
# PROFESSOR NOTE - server/.env.example
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT IS THIS FILE?
# This is a TEMPLATE. You copy it to a real file named ".env".
# The real ".env" holds SECRETS and is NEVER pushed to GitHub.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# YOUR HOMEWORK IN THIS FILE:
# 1. You will create a REAL file named ".env" next to this one.
# 2. You will copy-paste each line below into it.
# 3. You will replace the fake values with your REAL Atlas values.
# See Lesson 1 in chat for WHERE to get each value.
# ============================================================

# LESSON: MONGO_URI - the cloud address of your free database.
# WHAT TO PASTE: mongodb+srv://<your-user>:<your-password>@<your-cluster>.mongodb.net/portfolio?retryWrites=true&w=majority
# WHERE TO GET IT: Atlas Dashboard -> Connect -> Drivers -> Node.js -> copy string.
# PROFESSOR TIP: Keep "/portfolio" at end. That is your database name.

# MONGO_URI=PASTE_YOUR_ATLAS_STRING_HERE

# LESSON: PORT - which door your backend listens on.
# WHAT TO PASTE: 5000 (just use 5000 for this course).
# WHY: Your React runs on 5173, your backend runs on 5000. Two houses, two doors.

# PORT=5000

# LESSON: ADMIN_KEY - a simple secret password for YOUR admin panel.
# WHAT TO PASTE: Any long random word YOU invent, example: MySuperSecret12345!
# WHY: We will check this key before allowing Create/Update/Delete. No login system needed for Lesson 1.
# HOW YOU WILL USE IT: You type it in Admin panel, browser sends it as header "x-admin-key".

# ADMIN_KEY=PASTE_A_SECRET_YOU_INVENT_HERE

# LESSON: CLIENT_URL - where your frontend lives, so backend can allow it.
# WHAT TO PASTE for now: http://localhost:5173
# WHY: Browsers block strangers (CORS). This tells backend "trust my React".

# CLIENT_URL=http://localhost:5173
